From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:49:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] clocksource: Add the timer of the FonTamSOC ftpu

In machine mode, the CSR time of the ftpu counts every clock cycle, the
same on every hart, at the timebase; each hart compares it with its pair
of CSRs mtimecmp, 0x34d and 0x35d, which raise its machine timer
interrupt: a clocksource and sched_clock of 64 bits, and a oneshot
clockevent per cpu.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: William Tambe <tambewilliam@gmail.com>
